 evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPS-059"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-037", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-037: Sequence-memory lag effects with game-state controls", "score": 0.272, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-CHT-037 (0.19)", "FAM:SF-APPS-073 auto_related_family (limitation_precedent) FAM:SF-CHT-037"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Sequence-memory lag effects with game-state controls", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "Naive lag-1 play-type PPP effects survive period/clock/margin controls and within-team baselines.", "observed_result": "Lag-1 real, lag-2 small, lag-3+ ~0: d(1)=+0.024 AUC, d(2)=+0.004. SPOT_UP lag-1 MWU_p=0.0000 with and without controls. DRIVE lag-1 MWU_p=0.0000 but ctrl_p=0.0911. PNR naive p=0.031, controlled 0.136, within-team lift -0 [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)", "observed_failure_evidence": "DRIVE and PNR lag-1 effects disappear with game-state controls / within-team baseline.", "observed_sample_and_power": "NOT_RECORDED", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPS-073"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-CHT-029"}]}], "n_results": 4}

